  message: "Done in PR #2291 (dev 703dce32b; commits 35512a0d2 templates/bibtex/blade/handlebars/rust-analyzer refine, 0f2b88973 event-sourcing). Live on dev 703dce32b: hypergumbo survey on a fixture with refs.bib (@book{knuth:1984,...}), a Blade view (@extends('package::layouts.app')), Handlebars partials {{> shared/header}} and {{> ns:footer}}, and JS bus.on('user:created', ...) -> rc=0, validation_report.violations = 0. Ids: bibtex:refs.bib:1-1:knuth.1984:entry (name 'knuth:1984'), handlebars:hbs/page.hbs:2-2:ns.footer:partial (name 'ns:footer'), javascript:js/bus.js:4-4:user.created:function (name 'user:created'), Blade @extends dst blade:template:package::layouts.app:0-0:package..layouts.app:external_symbol; each id splits into 5 slots with the name slot free of ':'. Static: packages/hypergumbo-core/tests/test_id_newtypes.py:117 'HAND_BUILT_NODE_IDS ... = {}' (the table ends empty, as asked); test_id_newtypes.py passed in scripts/smart-test (mypy ratchet clean, 138 passed). Not exercised live by me: the view-template linker and rust-analyzer's refine_rust_kinds (no fixture/backend run); their re-mint is covered by the commit's measurement (aardvark-dns recording: 15 refined constants, 0 differ) and the empty table. Evidence: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/fast_smart_test_build_11172026/closure_pr3/rozod.txt, ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/fast_smart_test_build_11172026/closure_pr3/smarttest_core.txt"  # 9b96
